        "mark_note": "Labelled diagram",
        "why": "The Y shape shows at once why an antibody has two binding sites and one tail.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing the light chains as long as the heavy ones. They are shorter.",
          "Leaving the Fab and Fc ends unlabelled."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Two heavy chains make the Y; a light chain rides each arm.",
        "margin_note": "Label both ends and both chains.",
